Two separate questions:

1. Tab switching clears the result

The route result lives in React state — navigating away unmounts the component and the state is lost. Options:

Persist result to sessionStorage (simplest) — serialize the result on every change, rehydrate on mount. Survives tab switches within the same browser session.
Keep the component mounted, hide it — use CSS display:none instead of unmounting when switching tabs. Works but wastes memory.
Save to a route run and replay it — the infrastructure we just built actually handles this already for saved runs from the dashboard. Could wire the same loadSavedResult path after a fresh optimize too.
Recommendation: sessionStorage is the right tradeoff — simple, no server cost, clears when the browser closes.

2. PHI compliance

Current PHI exposure points:

patientName and address are stored in route_optimization_tasks (columns exist in schema, currently set to null on insert — good)
request_payload and result_payload in route_optimization_runs contain the full optimize request/response including patient names and addresses from the visits array
Audit logs may capture metadata with identifiable info
What needs to happen:

request_payload / result_payload: Either encrypt at rest (Neon supports transparent encryption) or strip patient names/addresses before storing — keep only patientId, visitId, coordinates
route_optimization_tasks: The patientName and address columns should stay null (already the case) or be dropped entirely (the deferred cleanup noted in memory)
Audit logs: Ensure no PHI leaks into metadata fields
Transport: Verify all API routes use HTTPS in prod (Vercel handles this)
Access control: Every endpoint already gates on auth.nurseId — good
The biggest risk right now is request_payload — it stores the full request including patientName fields for every visit. That's the first thing to address before any compliance claim.